  "body": "The [touch-action property](https://w3c.github.io/pointerevents/#the-touch-action-css-property) defines a number of tokens.  [Edge](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-ca/library/windows/apps/hh767313.aspx) and [Chrome](https://www.chromestatus.com/features/5670200775016448) also ship an additional `pinch-zoom` token (and I believe Firefox plans to as well /cc @staktrace).  But it's not clear if this [will ever make it into the W3C PointerEvents spec](https://github.com/w3c/pointerevents/issues/565).\r\n\r\nI think it's particularly important that we increase the visibility of this property (eg. [document it on MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/touch-action) for accessibility reasons.  Many image carousels already use `touch-action: pan-y` when they probably should be using `touch-action: pan-y pinch-zoom` in order to avoid disabling zooming for vision impared users.\r\n\r\nIt'll be a little awkward to monkey patch it in, but is it OK if I submit a PR for this?\r\n/cc @dtapuska @teddink @navidz @mustaqahmed",
